+Each fresh plan pays all ordinary length/modulus/generator, divisibility, representability/overflow and allocation guards. It also pays runtime omega^n and omega^(n/2) checks and, at n>=4, imag^2=-1, using the same checker for all schedules after omega/imag are available. Add those repeated check costs to the plan ledger separately from the source's n+35-log2(n) root-generation call count. Independently establishing primality, primitive-generator order and the mathematical root certificate is preflight audit work outside primary timing. p/g remain the pinned constants; an interface exposing them must reject wrong values. There is no uncharged per-plan verification hidden in the fixture stage.
 
